              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": null,
                "end_index": 119,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because vitamin B12 is a water-soluble vitamin, **there is currently no established Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL)**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 121,
                "end_index": 252,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The body typically absorbs only what it needs and excretes the excess through urine, making vitamin B12 toxicity exceptionally rare"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 256,
                "end_index": 380,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, taking extremely high doses of supplements or receiving frequent B12 injections can still occasionally cause issues"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 411,
                "end_index": 552,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Supplement Doses\n* **Daily Requirement:** The Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) for most healthy adults is **2.4 micrograms (mcg) per day**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 555,
                "end_index": 683,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Supplemental Doses:** Many over-the-counter supplements contain 1,000 mcg to 2,000 mcg\u2014which is thousands of times the RDA"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 685,
                "end_index": 838,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "High oral doses are generally safe and are often prescribed because the human digestive tract only absorbs a tiny fraction (about 1% or less) of oral B12"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 842,
                "end_index": 1188,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### Potential Side Effects of Excess B12\nWhile serious toxicity is highly unusual, prolonged megadoses or frequent therapeutic injections may lead to minor or moderate side effects, including:\n* **Dermatological Reactions:** The most common side effect of high B12 levels is skin issues, such as sudden acne-like breakouts or flare-ups of rosacea"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1190,
                "end_index": 1303,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Gastrointestinal Issues:** Some individuals experience mild nausea, diarrhea, or a temporary loss of appetite"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                4,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1305,
                "end_index": 1430,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Neurological & Other Symptoms:** Headaches, dizziness, or occasional tingling and numbness in the hands or feet can occur"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1433,
                "end_index": 1694,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### A Vital Clinical Distinction: Unexplained High B12 Levels\nIf a routine blood test reveals that your vitamin B12 levels are abnormally high, and you are **not** taking high-dose supplements or receiving injections, you should consult your healthcare provider"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1698,
                "end_index": 1822,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In the absence of supplementation, elevated blood levels of B12 (hypercobalaminemia) do not mean you are eating too much B12"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1824,
                "end_index": 1911,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, it can sometimes be an early marker of how your body is processing the vitamin"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1913,
                "end_index": 2097,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Your doctor will likely want to run follow-up tests to rule out underlying medical conditions, such as:\n* Liver disease (which can cause the liver to release stored B12 into the blood)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1913,
                "end_index": 2173,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Your doctor will likely want to run follow-up tests to rule out underlying medical conditions, such as:\n* Liver disease (which can cause the liver to release stored B12 into the blood)\n* Kidney dysfunction (which reduces the body's ability to clear excess B12)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1913,
                "end_index": 2214,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Your doctor will likely want to run follow-up tests to rule out underlying medical conditions, such as:\n* Liver disease (which can cause the liver to release stored B12 into the blood)\n* Kidney dysfunction (which reduces the body's ability to clear excess B12)\n* Certain blood or bone marrow disorders"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2216,
                "end_index": 2408,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### Next Steps\nIf you are currently taking a high-dose B12 supplement and are experiencing any unusual symptoms, or if you are unsure of your ideal dosage, it is best to speak with your doctor"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2410,
                "end_index": 2610,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "They can check your blood levels to help you determine whether you actually require supplementation, and tailor a safe, effective daily amount based on your individual dietary needs and health profile"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
